 "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet gateway (Fujitsu, multi-unit)",
 "applies_to": "Fujitsu VRF systems (outdoor units 0-11, indoor units 1-64) integrated through the Intesis 700 Series Air gateway IN775FGL***O000.",
 "summary": "The IN775FGL***O000 is a multi-protocol Intesis 700 Series gateway that reads a Fujitsu VRF network and serves it as BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP objects (the same map for both). It has gateway/batch objects, a block per outdoor unit and a block per indoor unit; instance numbers come from fixed formulas on the unit number.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Points are listed for the global/batch objects, outdoor unit 0 (OU block = (OU x 25) + 10000, OU 0-11) and indoor unit 1 (IU block = U x 100, U 1-64). Names keep the printed XX placeholder.",
  "The manual has no access column: _C (command) objects are taken as commandable, _S (status) objects as read-only.",
  "Batch_SetTemp_C is printed as object type \"1-Analog Input\". The manual's own type codes use 0 = Analog Input and 1 = Analog Output (every other _C setpoint is printed \"1-Analog Output\"), and it is a command, so AO 0 is used here.",
  "IUXX_FanSpeed_C/_S are printed twice with different state lists (7 speeds and 5 speeds) at the same instance; the 7-speed list is shown and the 5-speed list is in the description. Check which applies to your indoor units.",
  "Only the objects for units configured in the gateway exist; use IUXX_Exists_S to check."
 ],
